  "reviewScope": "Seven exact complete-paragraph source windows from five complete stories; original prose only, text stands without images or audio. Canonical whitespace and native paragraph boundaries retained. Home and nine original chapter author/licence footers inspected, no text exception found. No image, video, audio or caption admitted.",
  "supportReview": [
    "A New Flower: complete 145-word story A2; travel/flowers and Grandma/Dave references are explicit in prose; no image-dependent inference. Present-perfect never been is retained, not assigned to A1.",
    "Val first paragraph: 30 words A1/A2; short present-tense first-person statements introduce the neighbour and vegetables without requiring later death inference. First two paragraphs85 A2 keep She/ them antecedents and maybe uncertainty with their complete context. No later death inference is part of the scopes.",
    "Tree first three paragraphs103 A2 retain Randy, tree-search/mapping, reported height and logger threat. Hunt trees is clarified by immediately stated looking for big/old trees and making maps. Passive/reported wording remains intact; no task claims the reported tallest-tree status is verified current fact.",
    "Arctic third paragraph16 A1/A2 is three complete simple sentences about summer/ice/plants; no backward pronoun or image dependency. First five paragraphs112 A2 retain opening topic and cold/summer/moss/grouping context; idiomatic framing is not scored as a scientific fact.",
    "Existing beginner local hints, exact-source completion examples and source-order instruction are reused. Completion is word restoration; sequence is textual order, not semantic/chronological comprehension or calibrated CEFR.",
    "Grow Your Own Tomatoes: complete156-word A2 procedural article retains all four native list items,50cm pot depth, soil/window, planting,watering,light and ripeness. Full text does not require pictures. Exact-source word restoration/textual-order tasks retain imperative wording and do not assert horticultural or medical expertise."
